Description: An R port of the 'llm_judge_reporting' Python package
    accompanying Lee et al. (2025) <doi:10.48550/arXiv.2511.21140>. Corrects
    the bias of accuracy estimates obtained from an imperfect LLM judge using
    its estimated specificity and sensitivity, constructs confidence intervals
    that reflect uncertainty from both the test and the calibration data, and
    allocates a calibration budget between truly incorrect and truly correct
    items.
